-- title:
--   Exactness of the Dieudonné module functor at a kernel
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field of characteristic $p$ for a prime $p$, perfect in the sense that the $p$-power map on $k$ is bijective. Let $A'$ and $A$ be commutative $k$-algebras carrying cocommutative Hopf algebra structures over $k$ and finite-dimensional as $k$-modules, and assume that the Cartier duals [`CartierDual k A'`](def/HopfAlgebra_CartierDual.html#L12) and [`CartierDual k A`](def/HopfAlgebra_CartierDual.html#L12), namely the $k$-linear duals of $A'$ and $A$ with their convolution ring structures, are local rings. Let $B$ be a commutative $k$-bialgebra, let $\varphi \colon A' \to A$ be a bialgebra homomorphism and let $q \colon A \to B$ be a surjective bialgebra homomorphism whose kernel, as an ideal of $A$, is the ideal generated by the image under $\varphi$ of the augmentation ideal $\ker(\varepsilon_{A'})$ of $A'$. The conclusion is a conjunction about the Dieudonné modules $\mathrm{DieudonneModule}\ k\ p\ (-)$, the colimit over $n$ of the additive groups of those $x$ in $\mathrm{TruncatedWittVector}\ p\ n$ of the algebra in question which are primitive, i.e. satisfy $W_n(\Delta)(x) = W_n(\iota_1)(x) + W_n(\iota_2)(x)$ for the comultiplication $\Delta$ and the two inclusions into the tensor square: first, the additive map induced by $q$ is surjective; second, the pair consisting of the map induced by $\varphi$ followed by the map induced by $q$ is exact, i.e. the kernel of the latter is the image of the former.
--
--   This is the exactness of the contravariant Dieudonné functor $M(G) = \varinjlim_n \operatorname{Hom}(G, W_n)$ on finite commutative unipotent group schemes over a perfect field, in the form: if $\operatorname{Spec} B$ is the scheme-theoretic kernel of the homomorphism $\operatorname{Spec} A \to \operatorname{Spec} A'$ attached to $\varphi$, then $M(A') \to M(A) \to M(B) \to 0$ is exact. It is used in the constructions producing Hopf algebras, and towers of $p$-divisible type, with prescribed Dieudonné modules, and in the computation of the index of the image of Frobenius on a Dieudonné module.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Deformation_DieudonneModule_map_surjective_and_exact_map_of_ker_eq_map_ker_counit.lean

